# Working rules (Watch Later Extension v2)

Chrome/Edge MV3 extension. Source: `Watch Later Extension/`. Backend: Supabase project `ayzqfwtoeckgycmqzlve`. Full context lives in `project.mdc` — read it before touching auth, scheduling, or DB code.

## Scope

- v2 = same OAuth flow, token refresh, Calendar scheduling, history, referrals, analytics. Only the UI changes (`popup.html`, `style.css`, modal markup).
- Keep MV3 plain HTML/JS/CSS. No React/Vite/build tooling unless explicitly requested.
- Icons: Tabler icons only. Inline the SVG with `stroke="currentColor"` when a tint must come from CSS (`<img src>` can't be recolored).
- No hardcoded design values in v2 UI CSS: color, spacing, typography, radius, shadows, and schedule blurs must reference the Figma-derived CSS variables in the `:root` token block of `style.css` (`--color-*`, `--space-*`, `--type-*` / `--tracking-*`, `--radius-*`, `--shadow-*`, `--blur-sched-*`, `--font-condensed`, `--btn-h`). Typography is **Proxima Nova** (bundled TTFs in `fonts/`) — use `.text-*` utility groups, not inline `font-size`/`font-weight`. Never reintroduce Be Vietnam Pro or Barlow. Add a new token (named after the Figma style/variable) rather than inlining a value; one-off layout dimensions with no Figma token (e.g. card widths) are the only exception. Do not use `corner-shape` / corner smoothing.
- Overlay modals use the shared `.wl-modal` / `.wl-modal-panel` classes and `openOverlay()` / `closeOverlay()` — see **Motion** section for the full contract (easing, slide keyframes, exit hold rules, JS↔CSS pairs). Don't hand-roll another `is-open` + `hidden` toggle.
