## Figma → code (token-efficient UI workflow)

Decided 2026-08-27 after a slow Pain-screen pass burned tokens on the wrong tools. Follow this for every design tweak.

### Tool choice

| Change type | Do | Don't |
|---|---|---|
| 1–3 token tweaks (radius / stroke / type / spacing / color) | One focused Plugin dump (`use_figma` / Desktop Bridge) of the target node props → edit `:root` tokens → selfcheck → **measured** verify | `get_design_context` / design-to-code React+Tailwind dumps |
| New screen / layout rebuild | design-to-code skill + `get_design_context` OK, then **adapt** to existing tokens/components | Paste MCP React/Tailwind into this repo |
| Motion | Dump durations + live loop / CDP | Screenshot-caption parity as the pass/fail |

- Prefer Desktop Bridge / Plugin API property dumps over `get_design_context` for v2 UI tweaks.
- **Never** paste Figma MCP React/Tailwind output into this MV3 plain HTML/CSS/JS repo.
- Map to existing `:root` tokens in `style.css`; add a named token before hardcoding.
- Touch only files needed for the asked surface. No drive-by refactors.
- Optional: split into **inspect turn** (dump + proposed token diffs, no code) then **apply turn** (implement + selfcheck + measure).

### Scope contract (user prompts + agents)

Numbered ask is the contract. Do not expand into related "parity" fixes unless the user asks. Prefer this prompt shape:

```text
Scope (ONLY these):
1) …
2) …
3) …

Do NOT: rebuild the screen; change unrelated tokens; run get_design_context;
update docs unless a token/rule changed.

Parity = measured (computed style / selfcheck), not screenshot prose.
```

### Measure-first parity (before any screenshot)

1. Edit tokens / minimal CSS.
2. `node tests/selfcheck.js` from `Watch Later Extension/`.
3. Preview `http://localhost:8321/popup?preview=1` (+ flags). Prefer **one** static server on `:8321`.
4. CDP / `getComputedStyle` — assert radius, `fontSize`/`lineHeight`, borders, etc.
5. Screenshot only after measurements pass (optional visual sanity). **Do not** treat vision captions as ground truth when they contradict computed styles.

### Depth rule

- 1–3 token tweaks → dump → edit → measure → done.
- New screen / layout restructure → design context + dump + screenshot OK.
- Motion → dump durations + live loop only.

### Docs ritual

- Update `project.mdc` (facts + Last updated) and this file when a rule/token contract changes — **once at the end**, not mid-exploration.
- Grep tokens/selectors first; don't re-read whole `style.css` / `popup.js` unless needed.

## Auth invariants (breaking these caused the v1 re-login bug)

- `chrome.storage.local` is the ONLY source of truth for tokens. Both supabase-js clients must keep `persistSession: false, autoRefreshToken: false`.
- After EVERY successful refresh (background alarm or popup `setSession`), write the rotated token pair back via `persistSupabaseSession()`. Refresh tokens are single-use; a stale copy revokes the whole session.
- Never hard-logout on token expiry or a missing profile row — refresh/upsert first; logout only when every silent path fails or the user asks.
- **OAuth split (2026-08-30):** **Silent** Google OAuth runs in **background** only (`{ action: 'login', silent: true }`). **Interactive** consent runs in **popup** only (`lib/google-oauth.js` → `launchGoogleWebAuthFlow({ silent: false })` → `{ action: 'completeLogin', id_token, access_token }`). Never route interactive login through background — Chrome allows only one `launchWebAuthFlow` at a time.
- **`auth_oauth_lock`** in `lib/google-oauth.js` serializes every `launchWebAuthFlow` across popup + background (incl. 50-min alarm Google refresh via `enqueueOAuthFlow`). Popup retry once on `flow_busy`.
- Google token renewal: `launchWebAuthFlow` with `prompt=none, interactive:false` first; interactive consent is the last resort. Never use `chrome.identity.getAuthToken` (Chrome-only, breaks Edge).
- Client ships the anon key only; service role stays inside Edge Functions.

## Domain rules

- Max video length 3 hours; skip scheduling during YouTube ads.
- Video duration for the pill / slot math: prefer `.ytp-time-duration` and `ytInitialPlayerResponse.videoDetails.lengthSeconds` over `<video>.duration` (ads make `video.duration` lie).
- Referral email goes to the referrer only, never the redeemer.
- Table names are exact: `users`, `videohistory` (incl. `watched_at`, `forced`, `removed`, multi-session `session_group_id` / `session_index` / `session_count` / `video_offset_*` / `all_sessions_watched`), `feedback`, `button_clicks`, `referral_codes`, `referral_redemptions`, `user_slot_preferences` (the only prefs table), `calendar_slot_scores`, `calendar_scan_runs`, `slot_algorithm_config`, `queue_intercept_state`. `UserTokens` and `UserSlots` were removed; never recreate token backups or prefs dual-writes. The old `Users` typo shipped a production bug.
- Public schema security: every table must keep RLS enabled; extension policies are explicitly `TO authenticated` and use `(select auth.uid())`; `anon` has no public-table grants. Preserve the column-limited `users` grants so other users' email/avatar cannot be fetched. Reporting views are dashboard/service-role only.
- Slot prefs: never overwrite `selected_days`/`selected_times` on rescan — only first empty selection gets algorithm suggestions, **except** `triggeredBy: 'prefs-banner'` (prefs scan banner **Click here**). Scores live in `calendar_slot_scores`.
- Calendar scan: a freeBusy call that fails must throw, never return `[]` — an empty busy array is scored as "free all week", so a swallowed 403 hands the user invented slots. Only score ranges that actually came back (`coveredRanges`). After changing `lib/slot-algorithm.js` or the scan path, run `node tests/slot-algorithm-stress.js` as well as the selfchecks.

## Edge Function invariants (a 2026-08-05 pass found four live, exploitable orphans)

- **`verify_jwt: true` is not authentication.** It only proves the caller sent a JWT signed by this project, and the anon key ships inside the extension. Every function must call `auth.getUser()` itself and act on `user.id`.
- **Never trust the request body for identity or authorisation.** Derive the actor from the JWT and everything else from rows that belong to that actor. `sendreferralnotification` took `referrerId`/`friendName` from the body and became a "mail anyone arbitrary HTML from our domain" endpoint.
- **Escape every interpolated value in outbound email HTML.** Display names come from Google profiles.
- **Anything that sends mail needs an idempotency key** (e.g. `referral_redemptions.notified_at`), or a caller can replay it and mailbomb a user on our Resend quota.
- **CORS**: return `Access-Control-Allow-Origin` only for `chrome-extension://hkekbdlgnmjpbaijipkanenaeabhegfk` (+ `Vary: Origin`). Never reflect the request Origin, never `*`.
- **Don't leave orphan functions deployed.** An unused slug is still a public route: retire the body and delete the slug. Never deploy anything holding the Google client secret or a service-role key behind `verify_jwt: false`.

## Extension-page invariants

- The popup is a privileged page. Anything from another user, the DB, or a YouTube page goes in via `textContent`, or through `escapeHistoryHtml` if it must be `innerHTML`. CSP blocks injected script but not injected markup.
- URLs rendered into an `href` go through `safeExternalUrl` — escaping does not stop a `javascript:` URL firing on click.
- `chrome.runtime.onMessage` must reject foreign senders (`sender.id !== chrome.runtime.id`); without `externally_connectable`, web pages can't reach us but other extensions can.
- Auth parameters (nonce/state) use `crypto.randomUUID()`, never `Math.random()`.
- No `web_accessible_resources` unless a web page genuinely needs the file; extension pages load their own assets via `chrome.runtime.getURL` without it, and a WAR entry lets every site fingerprint the extension.

- `scanAndScore` is written but **not deployed** — don't deploy it, and don't "simplify" its timezone handling. Edge Functions run in UTC, so bucket boundaries must go through `tz.mjs`; `setHours()` there silently writes every score into the wrong bucket. `lib/slot-algorithm.js` is the reference implementation — change it first, then mirror into the function.
- The 2 open Supabase security warnings (leaked password protection, Postgres patch level) are **platform settings, not code**. They cannot be fixed by a migration or MCP call — see the table in `project.mdc`. Don't re-investigate them as bugs.

